Neither kit is modified. Neither makes a network request.

The bundled entries
-------------------

The bundle is a starter set of seven symbols and seventeen entries. Each entry is one tradition's
reading of one symbol, attributed to a named general reference work (Encyclopaedia Britannica, by
article title). The entries contain no quotations and no page numbers, because a citation this project
cannot verify to the page is not a citation.

Every entry is an ATTRIBUTION, not a fact. A tradition's reading of a symbol is a claim about what people
have made of it, and readings differ between scholars of the same tradition. The app says this on its
own face, and the same symbol in two cultures is kept as two entries rather than merged into one meaning.

Where the bundle is thin — and it is thin — the honest thing is to say so: seven symbols is a
demonstration of the structure, not a dictionary.
